elements.plainText:
Here is how different sound frequencies are represented by brain stem neurons:
at very low frequencies, phase locking is used; 
at intermediate frequencies, both phase locking and tonotopy are useful;
at high frequencies (5 kHz) tonotopy must be relied on to indicate sound frequency.

